$ enola upgrade --help
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
Usage: enola upgrade

Download and install the latest enola release, replacing the running
binary in place. A dev build is always treated as out of date. An
install managed by a package manager (pip, for one) is left alone, with
the command that upgrades it instead. Afterwards the new binary fetches
the Rubydex library it pins (`providers fetch rubydex`); a failure there
is reported and the upgrade still succeeds. ENOLA_NO_RUBYDEX_FETCH=1
skips it.

Exit codes:
  0  upgraded, already current, or left to the package manager
  1  the upgrade failed

Examples:
  # Replace this binary with the latest release
  enola upgrade

  # Which version is running
  enola --version

See also: enola help doctor
